th","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered MariaDB/data state, and restored replication; a final post-restart insert confirms end-to-end recovery.","limitations":["The first read-only probe reported an inconsistent displayed value of 0 and did not capture its error text, although immediate diagnostics and a repeated application-style probe directly showed read_only=ON and error 1290; this slightly reduces confidence.","After node1 restarted, node2 initially remained in a transient reconnect state and required an explicit I/O-thread restart before returning healthy. Recovery was subsequently demonstrated, so this does not negate the task outcomes or restart protocol.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inspect database contents; database correctness relies on the captured executor SQL observations."]}
